## Problem
Subscribe-daemon opens one reconnect loop per alias with no global limit on concurrent in-flight `/ws/subscribe` attempts. Under outage, all aliases connect in parallel → FD/thread pressure on the client and thundering herd on the server.

Live: one daemon hit ~200 ESTAB + 464 threads + 531MB RSS during a 502 window.

## Solution
1. Cap concurrent in-flight WS connects per daemon (queue remaining aliases).
2. Optionally cap total live WS sessions if product allows (or document multi-alias expected cost).
3. Tests: with N aliases and hung peer, concurrent connects ≤ cap.

## Files
- `ocaml/cli/c2c_relay_subscribe_daemon.ml`

## Related
B270. Server-side caps are a separate bug; both should land.